# Production ECS Architecture

Target: mature, extensible DOTS architecture for a large city-survival sim.

## Layers

```
Presentation (UI, camera, FMOD, VFX)
  → intents only
Application (thin): Intent → Command
  → no economy math
Simulation (ECS): source of truth
Content: Authoring/Baker, blobs, prefabs, balance tables
```

## Simulation domains (folders + SystemGroups)

Time → Commands → Workforce/Assignment → Production → Needs/Survival → Society/Laws → Gods/Crisis → WinLose → EmitEvents

## Rules

- One write model: ECS simulation world
- Systems = domain rules; components = state; avoid rich OO aggregates on entities
- Player/UI writes **commands**, not stocks directly
- Singletons for global state (`GameTime`, ledgers, phase) — not VContainer in core
- DI only optional in Presentation/Infrastructure (UI, FMOD, save)
- ScriptableObjects/authoring = design-time; runtime truth = entities/blobs
- Start workforce as **aggregates** (`AssignedCount`); agents/pathfinding later
- Prefer data-driven content for new buildings/resources/laws

## Anti-patterns

- `Button.onClick` computing production
- God `IEconomyService` used by UI and systems alike
- Mixing jam card architecture into ECS core
- Burst systems calling managed UI/FMOD directly
